{"id": "EUVD-2026-107352", "enisaUuid": "b641dfb0-c5cf-3d1c-a2cf-37343c988b64", "description": "Multiple Cisco products are affected by a vulnerability in the memory management implementation of Snort 3 that could allow an unauthenticated, remote attacker to cause the Snort 3 Detection Engine to restart, resulting in an interruption of packet inspection.\r\n\r\nThis vulnerability is due to incomplete error checking when Snort 3 processes files, which could cause unreleased memory. An attacker could exploit this vulnerability by sending a large number of files to be processed. A successful exploit could allow the attacker to cause the Snort 3 Detection Engine to restart unexpectedly, resulting in a DoS condition.", "datePublished": "2026-10-21T16:17:23", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-22T19:11:31", "baseScore": 5.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:C/C:N/I:N/A:L", "references": ["https://sec.cloudapps.cisco.com/security/center/content/CiscoSecurityAdvisory/cisco-sa-snort3-misc-dos-6mB22qAK"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-76489", "GHSA-4m4m-399q-8257"], "assigner": "cisco", "epss": 0.32, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "01a3613d-7ae3-35e6-864f-d79d99db1f3f", "product": {"name": "Cisco Open Source Snort3", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "3.1.63.0"}, {"id": "02b7f94b-c88a-305c-8d90-02d65c2f58a0", "product": {"name": "Cisco Open Source Snort3", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "3.1.45.0"}, {"id": "04914165-2755-3587-a0cd-7f5a9d1001d1", "product": {"name": "Cisco Secure Firewall Threat Defense (FTD) Software", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "7.7.10"}, {"id": "079a9725-6d66-3f83-b53a-30a72114d767", "product": {"name": "Cisco Secure Firewall Threat Defense (FTD) Software", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "10.0.0"}, {"id": "0b41e9d4-81c5-363a-957e-a760f51d235e", "product": {"name": "Cisco Secure Firewall Threat Defense (FTD) Software", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version"